            <ArticleTitle>Laser utilization in the oral pharynx.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>963-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the past three decades, the surgical laser has evolved into an invaluable tool in the practice of otolaryngology-head and neck surgery with many applications in the treatment of oropharyngeal lesions. The use of lasers has allowed many of these lesions to be treated effectively in the office setting with minimal patient discomfort. These applications are reviewed, and the advantages and shortcomings of laser use in the oropharynx are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
